From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tristin Baker <tristinbaker@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:43:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Draw the custom cursor in the main menu, load screen and
 party creation

With OE_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_MOUSE there's no system cursor, and only the game loop and the game menu drew the game's
own: in the main menu, its load screen, the credits and party creation the cursor was invisible, so neither the
touchpad nor the d-pad menu navigation could be followed there.

Mouse look now only comes back when the game's own interface is the one window, as the comment says, not with any
single window such as the main menu.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Application/Game.cpp       | 5 +++++
 src/GUI/UI/UIPartyCreation.cpp | 3 +++
 src/Io/Mouse.cpp               | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Application/Game.cpp b/src/Application/Game.cpp
index 9b64aa4..a2d4b56 100644
--- a/src/Application/Game.cpp
+++ b/src/Application/Game.cpp
@@ -142,6 +142,11 @@ int Game::run() {
                 // This method should be interpreted as a future RetainedUISystem::update()
                 // It does update all the GUIWindow alive + it does various hacks
                 GUI_UpdateWindows();
+#ifdef OE_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_MOUSE
+                // No system cursor to show in the main menu, load screen and credits, the game draws its own.
+                if (current_screen_type != SCREEN_VIDEO)
+                    mouse->DrawCursor();
+#endif
                 render->flushAndScale();
                 engine->drawOverlay();
                 render->swapBuffers();
diff --git a/src/GUI/UI/UIPartyCreation.cpp b/src/GUI/UI/UIPartyCreation.cpp
index 284caaf..59a3f6a 100644
--- a/src/GUI/UI/UIPartyCreation.cpp
+++ b/src/GUI/UI/UIPartyCreation.cpp
@@ -725,6 +725,9 @@ bool PartyCreationUI_LoopInternal() {
         CreateParty_EventLoop();
         render->BeginScene2D();
         GUI_UpdateWindows();
+#ifdef OE_GAMEPAD_TOUCHPAD_MOUSE
+        mouse->DrawCursor(); // No system cursor, the game draws its own.
+#endif
         render->Present();
         if (uGameState ==
             GAME_FINISHED) {  // if click Esc in PlayerCreation Window
diff --git a/src/Io/Mouse.cpp b/src/Io/Mouse.cpp
index 33f9546..a665a18 100644
--- a/src/Io/Mouse.cpp
+++ b/src/Io/Mouse.cpp
@@ -131,7 +131,7 @@ void Io::Mouse::DrawCursor() {
     Pointi pos = this->position();
 
     // manage mouse look state - if only game screen is active and no overlay (console) is open, try enable
-    if (lWindowList.size() == 1 && !engine->isOverlayOpen())
+    if (lWindowList.size() == 1 && lWindowList.front() == pPrimaryWindow.get() && !engine->isOverlayOpen())
         RestoreMouseLook();
     else
         SetMouseLook(Suspended);
